jenkins and github


Github repo and jenkins integretion 


1. Generate a Fresh Token in GitHub

Go to GitHub → Settings → Developer Settings → Personal Access Tokens → Tokens (classic).

Click Generate new token (classic).

Check the repo scope box (critical for repository access).

Click Generate token and copy it.

--------------------------------------------------------

2. Update the Credential in Jenkins


Do not create a new credential; modify the existing one so your code doesn't have to change.

Open Jenkins and go to Manage Jenkins → Credentials.

Click on the Global domain.

Find the credential ID you used (e.g., github-jenkins-token) and click the Update icon (pencil tool) on the right side.

Keep your Username exactly as your GitHub username (githubuser id).

Clear the Password field and paste your new GitHub Personal Access Token.

Click Save



